    "label": "40",
    "prompt": "Find rational $a$ and $b$ such that\n$$(1+\\sqrt3)^4=a+b\\sqrt3.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=28,\\quad b=16$",
      "worked": "Using Pascal coefficients $1,4,6,4,1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(1+\\sqrt3)^4&=1+4\\sqrt3+6(3)+4(3\\sqrt3)+9\\\\(1+\\sqrt3)^4&=28+16\\sqrt3\\end{align*}$$\nComparing rational and surd terms gives $a=28$ and $b=16$.",
